/Title (Read the diagonal:  a calibrated model's curve lies on it. Every raw curve \(grey\) sits above: the 2015 vintage defaulted more than the training years, so all models under-predict PD. Raw trees are worst:  ECE 0.034 vs the scorecard's 0.025; margin-maximizing ensembles are not probability models. Isotonic recalibration helps everyone  but cannot anticipate drift that was not yet visible in 2014. The scorecard stays best-calibrated:  ECE 0.0175 vs XGBoost's 0.0214 after identical recalibration. The trees keep the better Brier score, which also rewards discrimination.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 457 0 R
>>
endobj
490 0 obj
<<
/Title (scikit-learn XGBoost LightGBM SciPy)
