503 0 obj
<<
/Title (Statistically decisive:  283,026 test loans give enormous power; the boosted-tree edge is unambiguous. Economically modest:  +0.85 AUC points, not the +8 to +15 sometimes quoted from random-split studies. Deep learning does not pay:  the MLP is significantly worse than the forty-year-old scorecard, on tabular credit data.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 496 0 R
/Prev 511 0 R
>>
endobj
504 0 obj
<<
/Title (data  loaders + leakage whitelist + vintage split woe / scorecard  WoE binning, IV screen, logistic, points scaling models  XGBoost, LightGBM, MLP on a shared design matrix calibration  Platt + isotonic, fit on the 2014 vintage metrics  AUC, KS, Brier, ECE, DeLong test, bootstrap CIs decision  accept/reject profit sweep over PD cutoffs pipeline  end-to-end orchestration, 5 seeds per ML model)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 497 0 R
/Next 505 0 R
>>
endobj
505 0 obj
<<
/Title (The baseline is honest:  an industry-style weight-of-evidence scorecard, not a strawman logistic regression on raw inputs. Same information for everyone:  all four models see the identical 23 origination-time features; preprocessing differences cannot explain gaps. Calibration is separated from fitting:  every model is recalibrated the same way on the validation vintage, mimicking bank practice. Profit uses real cash flows:  repaid loans earn their actual interest; charged-off loans lose 65% of principal.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 497 0 R
/Prev 504 0 R
/First 512 0 R
/Last 512 0 R
/Count -1
>>
endobj
